# Trivy vulnerability suppressions for the backend image scan (backend/cloudbuild.yaml
# `scan-image` step). Each entry MUST carry a dated justification and a removal
# condition. Suppress ONLY non-reachable findings; never silence an exploitable one.

# CVE-2026-47884 — spring-webmvc 6.2.19 (via Spring Boot 3.5.14).
# CRITICAL RCE "via improper path limitation in XsltView". Not reachable in this
# service: the backend is a pure JSON REST API (73 @RestController, 0 @Controller)
# and uses NO server-rendered views — no XsltView / InternalResourceView / JSP /
# FreeMarker view resolution anywhere, so the vulnerable code path is never invoked.
# Trivy's only fixed version is 7.0.9 (Spring Framework 7 / Spring Boot 4), a major
# breaking upgrade tracked separately.
# Added 2026-10-06. REMOVE once the Spring Boot 4 upgrade lands (spring-webmvc >= 7.0.9).
CVE-2026-47884
